{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T17:23:32.952Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1775"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1775: the secret guard flags bare environment-variable references (api_key: ${API_KEY}) as credentials since the #1704 widening"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1775 (filed 2026-11-23 while moving the extension package pm-memory to 2026.11.23; draft unbraind/pm-memory#96 is blocked on it). Since the credential-key guard widened beyond password (pm-gh1704), scanMutationSecrets reports credential_key_assignment for a value made only of a reference under a credential key: scanMutationSecrets(JSON.stringify({ title: 'api_key: ${API_KEY}', updated: '2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z' })) returns [] on 2026.11.14 and a credential_key_assignment finding on 2026.11.23. A reference names where a secret lives and holds no secret value, so trackers that document configuration (api_key: ${API_KEY}, token=$GITHUB_TOKEN) have their mutations refused. pm-hw00c2 (closed) made CREDENTIAL_VALUE capture a value that holds a run-time reference whole and judge the literal left after expansion; a bare reference leaves no literal, so whether it should still match is the question this item settles. Expected: a value made only of a reference (${NAME}, $NAME, ${{ secrets.NAME }} and similar) is not a credential under any credential key; a reference with an attached literal or a literal value is still flagged. Duplicate check: searched secret guard environment variable reference credential key bare reference; pm-hw00c2, pm-ycgb5g and pm-gh1704 are closed and own the literal-concatenation and key-widening rules."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1775","regression","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T17:23:32.952Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T17:23:32.952Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Bare references under api_key, client_secret, token, secret and password produce no finding in JSON, YAML, dotenv, XML and quoted-key forms; Attached literals and literal values are still flagged; A corpus test pins both sides, with the 2026.11.23 behaviour as the negative control"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Reference-only configuration values pass the secret guard while literal credentials stay refused"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1704","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-23T17:23:32.952Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-hw00c2","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-23T17:23:32.952Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"fe7c2fb0d2aef7352bd3183e78823ddb6c20b1c89d357d