{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T21:30:49.227Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T21:30:49.227Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-23T21:30:49.227Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause (2026-11-23, reproduced on the 2026.11.23 build and compared with 2026.11.14 in a scratch prefix): the false positive needs a SIBLING member after the string that holds the assignment. With the title alone the scan is clean; with any later member it flags. The flat scan reads the serialized JSON text, and both key-named value grammars (credential_key_assignment and password_assignment) read a quoted piece after a reference as a shell concatenation. So the closing quote of the enclosing JSON string, the comma and the next key's opening quote form a quoted piece whose body is only a comma, and the literal judged after reference expansion becomes comma + next key + colon + next value. A 588-case grid (7 keys x 7 reference spellings x 12 forms) measured 98 false positives on main: braced, defaulted and angle references in compact JSON text, arrays, nested objects and Python-repr text for every key, plus password with a bare dollar-name or command reference in the same forms (wordComplete treats any quote after an unquoted value as a possible concatenation, so the dollar-name stays literal), plus password with a bare Windows percent-name in every form (flagged on 2026.11.14 too; the credential-key rule already treats it as a placeholder). Fix plan: a quoted piece whose body is only JSON structure punctuation is a string boundary, never a concatenated piece, in both grammars; wordComplete treats the same boundary after an unquoted value as the end of its word; a whole-value percent-name is a reference for every key-named rule."}]}],"before_hash":"82ce4815212ad941e23f077a3decf9571631d86eed9be6848459ab68127a4d2c","after_hash":"095a894132bface8f9a1cd588cae0bf8b9af3a7f3e091e1e23295e2b2c184e61","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"16c864b8682421c3d548a263e384463d5f5ba07f79cc43dea8ec9e2247a69d6d"}
