{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T21:44:27.868Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"tests_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T21:44:27.868Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/security","scope":"project","timeout_seconds":600,"provenance":{"author":"harness:claude-code","created_at":"2026-11-23T21:44:27.654Z","source_kind":"local_mutation","source_ref":"fix/secret-guard-string-boundaries-spaced-userinfo"}}]}],"before_hash":"9be48bbff30965e76def46fba8b3cfc7bbfa58a1e59e662f2dde40f76da21856","after_hash":"bdbfb601de3803c0d50cf4c8c684d9709455591f0934d75ba29f5661677b7f94","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"94be50c290db869a92f7fd80075f5320e71dde9a4ab08151d037df0bf77a2547"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T21:51:17.775Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T21:51:17.774Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Decision note (2026-11-23): two pins from the pm-hw00c2 review loop (Codex round 10) are reversed on purpose. They kept a CONSTANT_CASE dollar-name literal whenever any quote followed an unquoted password value, even where that quote closes the enclosing string (a JSON array element followed by a sibling, and a JSON member value ending the object), and a cut-reference linear-time input counted one finding for the same reason. GH-1775 requires those JSON forms to be clean. The new rule (closesEnclosingString) ends the word only when the quote is followed by blanks and a line break or the end of the text, or by JSON structure, optional blanks and the next member or element; the Codex round 10 passphrase case (a quote followed by a space and words) still keeps the variable literal and is still reported. The differential over 3,952 cases against the published 2026.11.23 bundle gained no finding; every lost finding is a bare reference, a whole-value percent name, or the residual (19) shape recorded on pm-jcz7qz."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T21:51:17.775Z"}],"before_hash":"bdbfb601de3803c0d50cf4c8c684d9709455591f0934d75ba29f5661677b7f94","after_hash":"a3b32ab223acbc630d164562a0ea13956d432514976baddfba264285e30c24c9","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c5706632dc25d2ecc54d2a4e88864023f88b3330e96a908626b75d53298c834e"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T22:40:05.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T22:40:05.298Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Redesign after Codex review round 1 (2026-11-23, 12 findings, 4 P1). The first approach guessed from local shapes whether a quote closes an enclosing string (a structure run and a next string that closes within 4,096 characters). Codex showed it misreads YAML doubled single quotes, accepts a quote no string opened (a YAML plain scalar ending in a double quote), misses JSON whitespace before a separator, and flips verdicts when the next member is longer than the bound. Replaced by a lexical rule: flatMatches computes the string state before every position in one linear pass per scan (quote opens or closes its own kind, the other kind is data, backslash escapes, line breaks end strings); when a key-named rule's value sits in an open string whose closing quote lies inside or right after the capture and a word end follows that quote (whitespace, end of text, or structure then the next member, element, line break or end), the match is truncated there, wordComplete treats that quote as the end of the word, and the scan resumes at the quote so keys in later members are still scanned. The regex grammar is identical to main again. The whole-value Windows percent-name addition was dropped (it was not a whole-value check, and the issue does not require it; recorded as residual 20 on pm-jcz7qz). Measured after the redesign: grid 0 false positives outside the dropped percent case; differential over 3,952 cases versus 2026.11.23 gains 12 true positives (literals attached to a reference inside a Python-repr string) and loses only bare references, sibling-swallowing cases, and residual 18; scans stay linear (6M characters in 1.7 s, doubling per size step)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T22:40:05.298Z"}],"before_hash":"a3b32ab223acbc630d164562a0ea13956d432514976baddfba264285e30c24c9","after_hash":"9ba21062914a369c171bedd64f3cb2c2428f4d38672957ea1c4c7878ffbaea17","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"295082d3f6c557f61559b209bf17e315cce014036f14a54f84a0c92a26614699"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T22:56:19.475Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T22:56:19.474Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 (2026-11-23): a prose apostrophe (customer's) opened a string in the lexical pass, so a quoted password after it read as the closing quote and was dropped; a quote right after a letter, digit or underscore no longer opens a string. The Windows percent-name is now implemented as a whole-value check rather than dropped: unquoted text is whole only when blanks then a line break or the end follow it, or when it ends at the string it sits in; quoted values, decoded literals and element bodies are whole by construction; a dotenv or set line with more words after the reference stays reported. The credential-key reference-free grammar now excludes a percent-name only when it ends the value, so a literal attached to it is reported (main missed it). Grid: 0 false positives over every key, reference (percent-name included) and form. Differential versus 2026.11.23: 126 gained true positives (attached literals after a percent-name or inside a Python-repr string), losses limited to bare references, sibling-swallowing cases and residual 18."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T22:56:19.475Z"}],"before_hash":"9ba21062914a369c171bedd64f3cb2c2428f4d38672957ea1c4c7878ffbaea17","after_hash":"8b72fa3c8d46a45d04316d35eaf0a6aa3c20890d93cb511a6892a173541937d9","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"94624265af36cb2249a50213753424db5c5956cec14f1772f982f0550c35e7ae"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T23:10:34.083Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T23:10:34.082Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 (2026-11-24): fixed a regression where a YAML flow apostrophe (a plain note scalar holding an apostrophe before a password key) made the password's own opening quote read as the enclosing closer; a value is never cut at its own first character, which keeps main's reading there (and keeps the empty-assignment JSON shape flagged as main does). U+2028 and U+2029 no longer end a string in the lexical pass (JSON allows them raw); a closing quote followed by an XML tag end or by structure and an unquoted YAML flow key now ends the word; blanks after the structure are padding however many. Residual recorded: multi-line double-quoted YAML scalars (a raw line feed inside the string) still end the string state at the line feed."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T23:10:34.083Z"}],"before_hash":"8b72fa3c8d46a45d04316d35eaf0a6aa3c20890d93cb511a6892a173541937d9","after_hash":"90371b5c4eb8455a513641073216314f94b81fd1d81d344325d4d669140290b1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"cacb4cad117165b4ca82f5cf03aaee1c8fefc055c188224bd0d2a2a457c3ecaf"}
